# SP2 step 2: the bootstrap configuration keeps its state in the bucket it made.
# Format: file | regular expression the file must contain | message if it doesn't
terraform/bootstrap/backend.tf | ^[[:space:]]*backend "s3" \{ | the bootstrap config needs an S3 backend of its own
terraform/bootstrap/backend.tf | ^[[:space:]]*key[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*"bootstrap/terraform\.tfstate"$ | its own key, so the pipeline destroy in SP14 cannot reach it
terraform/bootstrap/backend.tf | ^[[:space:]]*use_lockfile[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true$ | native locking, not a DynamoDB table
terraform/bootstrap/backend.tf | ^[[:space:]]*encrypt[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*true$ | state objects are encrypted at rest
